{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1792892424278321001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"pelage-squishy-cony","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":2},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1792886262507592001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7e19b423-4314-4cb0-9d48-1582a67fe80a","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"d909-5158-adab-4fe7"}],"description":"## Observation\nFound while investigating bug d909-5158-adab-4fe7 (2026-10-24, code reading only; not reproduced). In `src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py`, the foreign-principal path of `_opcert_trust_root` uses `_pinned_environment_keys`, which returns every keyring entry with a public key, including entries whose `revoked_at_log_position` is set. `verify_opcert_record` has no tickets-log position for the certificate, so it cannot apply the era checks (`added_at_log_position` / `revoked_at_log_position`, verdict `key_not_valid_at_era`) that `verify_required_environment` applies.\n\n## Hypothesis\nA certificate signed by a key after its revocation, or before it was pinned, verifies as certified on this path. Unproven: a test with a revoked pinned key for a foreign principal would show it.\n\n## Approach\nReproduce with a pin file holding a revoked key and a certificate signed under it for a foreign principal. If it verifies, decide between refusing revoked keys outright (simple) and threading the certificate's log position through so eras apply (larger; changes a shared verification signature), then fix with a test.\n\n## Testing\n```\npytest tests/unit/test_opcert_local_verify_binding.py -q\n```\nFailure case: the revoked-key certificate is expected to be rejected after the fix.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The behaviour for a revoked pinned key of a foreign principal is reproduced and recorded (checked: new test result in a ticket comment).\n- [ ] A certificate signed under a revoked pinned key no longer verifies as certified on the foreign-principal path (checked: new test, which fails on main if the hypothesis holds).\n","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["opcert","security","verification"],"ticket_id":"0ed1-128f-b9a5-4c39","ticket_type":"bug","title":"verify_opcert_record trusts revoked pinned keys for a foreign principal and checks no key era","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["9339f355-1808-4c17-88d2-8535944c126a","7e19b423-4314-4cb0-9d48-1582a67fe80a"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1792892424278321001,"uuid":"daef49fd-f2c2-427b-b753-ec8f1558dad6"}